  "limitations": [
    "Timing covers a single source-way physical-sign candidate query, not map matching, geometry projection, full bounded graph traversal, display, or cold-cache/device latency.",
    "The current association index restricts way/direction/status but not station range; ORDER BY station requires a temporary B-tree. Measured per-way cardinality is reported rather than asserting strict station-range complexity.",
    "Physical source station anchors are mandatory: traffic_sign_way_rule continuation rows start at an interval boundary and are not physical sign locations.",
    "Relation groups are undirected endpoint-connected sets: builder drops relation member ordering and member roles; relation identity alone cannot select a future branch.",
    "Base-only v3 does not retain full motorcar permitted directions, lanes, or maxspeed:conditional metadata; optional traffic_sign_way_direction adds them. No safe exact-sign forecast should be claimed from maxspeed-tag-only segment boundaries.",
    "The separate v4 benchmark lacks continuity/endpoints/runtime and is not a substitute for v3 runtime capability.",
    "Prototype SQL finds candidate numeric signs only. Production selector must also stop at an earlier contextual/end/conflicting event, suppress ambiguous branches and intervening applicability changes, validate match/direction confidence, and compare against the authoritative current effective limit.",
    "way_links and way_endpoints are constructed only from rounded start/end coordinates. They omit source OSM node identity, interior junction incidence, grade/layer incidence semantics and turn-restriction relations; a unique outgoing endpoint candidate is not proof of a unique route continuation.",
    "traffic_sign_rule_path records the downstream propagation of an already-passed sign; it is not a proof of an upstream approach path toward an upcoming sign.",
    "Warm-cache sample generation first reads all qualified source signs. Measurement is intentionally an existence/efficiency check of indexed lookup, not a cache-cold benchmark.",
    "Unlocated or unknown-direction rejected signs cannot be safely assigned as directed barriers from current fields; source and applicability coverage remain incomplete."
  ],
